# `multitex.mtl` with one normal map added, for #1574.
#
# `beta` is the interesting entry: it shares `alpha`'s diffuse and differs
# ONLY in carrying a `map_bump`. That is what makes it bite — a merge guard
# keyed on the diffuse alone folds the two together, and a WebGPU bind-group
# key that does not separate normal maps hands one of them the other's.
newmtl alpha
Kd 1.0 0.2 0.2
map_Kd multitex-a.png

newmtl beta
Kd 0.2 1.0 0.2
map_Kd multitex-a.png
map_bump multitex-b.png

newmtl gamma
Kd 0.2 0.2 1.0
map_Kd multitex-b.png

newmtl plain
Kd 0.9 0.9 0.9
